  "configuration_id": "config_003",
  "reason": "With no completed experiments, there is no evidence to exploit, so the priority is establishing a clean reference point that maximizes the information value of subsequent ablations. config_003 (multimodal, singleprofile, scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, no aggregation, concat) is the simplest multimodal configuration using the most common encoders (scgpt for RNA, ViT-L for image) and the simplest fusion (concat). It directly tests the study's primary hypothesis—whether combining RNA and image modalities improves validation accuracy—while keeping the design space minimal (single profile, no aggregation) so that any performance can be cleanly attributed. The natural follow-up experiment (config_004, rna_only singleprofile scgpt) would then isolate the image contribution with a single-variable comparison. Starting here gives the highest-leverage baseline from which to build a structured ablation ladder across profile setting, encoder choice, aggregation, and fusion strategy under the limited budget."
}

